course: dictionary
lesson: 15408
title: The word spouse
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A spouse is the person you are married to. If your mum is married to your dad, your dad is her spouse. A spouse can be a husband or a wife.
explain: In everyday talk, people usually say husband, wife or partner. «Spouse» is the word you will see on forms, in law and in serious writing. A form that asks for «spouse or partner» wants the name of the person you are married to.
explain: Spouse is a noun, so you can have one spouse or two spouses. Test the meaning in a sentence: «Her spouse is kind» means her husband or wife is kind. If your meaning still fits, you have it right.
fact: A spouse is the person you are married to.
fact: «Spouse» means husband or wife, whatever their sex.
fact: «Spouse» is a formal word, used on forms and in law.
fact: «A surviving spouse» means a married person whose husband or wife has died.
fact: In everyday talk, people say husband, wife or partner instead.
exercise: «Mum filled in the form and wrote her spouse's name in the box.» What is a spouse? | Your older brother | A kind of form | *The person you are married to | Your best friend from school
exercise: On a form, which word means the person you are married to? | Spoon | Sparrow | Spotted | *Spouse
exercise: «Grandma is a surviving spouse, because her husband died.» What does surviving spouse mean? | A person who is very tired | A child who is still alive | A spouse who is getting married soon | *A married person whose husband or wife has died
test: «At the wedding, the bride and her spouse cut the big cake together.» Who is the spouse here? | *The person the bride is married to | The vicar who read the words | A baby sister | A guest who brought a present
test: Nadia says «spouse» is just a fancy word for «partner». Is she right? | Yes, they mean exactly the same in every sentence | No, a spouse is a child | *Not quite: a spouse is a married partner, a husband or wife | Yes, but only on the phone
exam: Ella's form asks, «Name of spouse?» What should she write? | The name of her school | The name of her pet | *The name of the person she is married to | The name of her favourite singer
